oduct	27	Once a definite idea for a new product has been accepted, a business proposal should be developed before _____  _____  _____.	12	.688533988170574	Disclaimer	36	A written statement added to a warranty that includes exceptions to and exclusions from the warranty is called a(n) _____.	13	.178377112922434	Evaluating Customer Acceptance	30	This last step of new product development involves how the market responded to the product.  This is accomplished through _____  _____  _____.	14	.167963708829118	Express Warranty	35	A manufacturer’s promise that is explicitly stated, in either writing or spoken word is called a(n) _____  ______.	15	.187313522765093	Fair Packaging and Labeling Act	42	There is a “Labeling Law” which was passed in 1966 under the recommendations of the Food and Drug Administration and the Federal Trade Commission.  It is  the ____  ____  ____  ____  ____.	16	.162945461069674	Full Warranty	34	This kind of warranty may state “If a product is found to be defective within the warranty period, it will be repaired or replaced at no cost to the original owner.”  It is called a(n) _____  _____.	17	.785398186084534	Generic Brandsor Generic	1	Products that carry no brand name and that are not promoted or advertised are called _____  _____.	18	.84481474330873	Growth Stage	46	Sales and profits increase during the points on a Product Life Cycle called the _____  _____.	19	.480461282879329	Implied Warranty	37	States may have their own laws indicating that a warranty exists automatically; this is called a(n) _____ _____.	20	.984136887352977	Installment Account	50	A credit arrangement that permits payment to be made over a specified period of time is referred to as a(n) _____  _____.	21	.486539031139826	Introduction Stage	29	The step of a Product’s Life Cycle where emphasis is on promotion and production is called the _____  _____.	22	.753446061980653	Label	31	Printed information that is either attached to or on a product for the customer’s convenience and/or safety is called a(n) _____.	23	.96605429098292	Limited Warranty	33	A warranty that does not cover full replacement of a product is a(n) _____  _____.	24	.392918748032729	Manufacturer Brand	8	A brand which belongs to and is promoted by the producer is called a(n) _____  _____.	25	.651471409318722	Maturity Stage	49	The stage of the Product Life Cycle when sales begin to level off or slow down is called the _____  _____.	26	.737816775095564	Mixed-Brand Strategy	9	A company that offers a combination of manufacturer, national, private, and generic brands is using _____-_____  _____.	27	.279976419769217	Obsolete	41	Goods that are no longer in demand and eventually become outdated are said to be _____.	28	.802175459359854	One	22	The development of new products involves several steps.  In order to come up with ideas for new products, creativity must be evident and would most likely be step number ______.	29	.601210079435823	Planograms	43	Diagrams created by computers that tell retailers how to display product items down both sides of an aisle at individual stores are called _____.	30	.624364198010584	Private Distributor Brandalso known asDealer Brand or Store Brand	7	A brand owned and initiated by wholesalers and retailers is known as a(n) _____  _____  _____.	31	.0555513459516463	Product Depth	18	The total amount of product items available within a product line refers to _____  _____.	32	.551857593260639	Product Item	16	Given a particular line of products, the make, model, brand, color, or size of any one product with that line is called a(n) _____  _____.	33	.448283950541301	Product Life Cycle	11	The stages that a good or service encounters over and over while it is available for sale is referred to as its _____  _____  _____.	34	.296510954991221	Product Line	17	Goods which come from the same manufacturer and are closely related such as all the Campbell’s™ Soups are part of the same _____  _____.	35	.308356747640463	Product Mix	13	All the goods that a company manufacturers or distributes are referred to as that company’s _____  _____.	36	.842372928206983	Product Modification	20	To change or alter a company's product(s) is called _____  _____.	37	.068839767979849	Product Packaging	15	The wrapping which may provide any or all of the following:  protection, identification, promotion, information, and utilization of the item being sold is called _____  _____.	38	.646126511807612	Product Planning	12	A manufacturer’s decisions about  ideas for new goods and services it creates in addition to all the steps from creation of the good or service to the satisfaction of customer needs is called _____  _____.	39	.45962053745036	Product Positioning	14	Manufacturers take special efforts to create a particular image for a good or service through promotion, price, quality, and service.  This is called _____  ______.	40	.761804374755269	Product Width	19	All the different kinds of closely related goods a business sells or manufactures make up a business’ _____  _____.	41	.070569931562324	Revolving Accounts	45	A store credit card where the retailer sets the credit limit and specifies when payments are due is called a(n) _____  _____.	42	.299725141981489	Screened	23	During this step of product development, new product ideas are either “accepted or eliminated” based on company objectives.  In other words, during this step, ideas are _____.	43	.537805077870286	Testing the Product	24	After a prototype, beta version, or the real product has been developed, a very expensive step that is sometimes bypassed because of the cost is _____  _____  _____.	44	.889943765890758	Trade Characters	21	Personalized brand marks that take on human-like personalities or become icons are called _____  _____.	45	.989980437322511	Trade Name	28	The legal name that a company or corporation uses, for identification purposes, when it does business is called its _____  _____.	46	.190739182844171	Trademark	25	A brand name, brand mark, trade character, insignia, or an emblem that is legally protected and identified with its own individuality is called a(n) _____.	47	.284873325976019	Warranty	32	A manufacturer’s promise or guarantee provided to a customer about the durability or deterioration of a particular product or service is called a(n) _____.	48	.474468549934434	Warranty of Fitness for a Particular Purpose	40	An implied warranty that creates action taken by the customer is called a(n) _____  _____  _____  ____  _____  _____  _____.	49	.105301491965214	Warranty of Merchantability	38	A promise from the seller that the product sold works for exactly what it says it works for is called a(n) _____   _____  _____.	50	.38866574149051	